    "result_text": "Build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI converted all rejection responses (400, 409, 429) to return RFC7807 `application/problem+json` bodies while keeping the HTTP status codes unchanged.\n\n**The mechanism:** In this OfficeFloor app, escalation handlers respond via `ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<T>>`, which OfficeFloor delegates to Spring's return-value handlers. Spring serializes a `ProblemDetail` body as `application/problem+json` automatically. A `ProblemDetails.build(...)` helper already existed and was used by the 400 `ValidationExceptionHandler` (and the 403/404/500 handlers). The rejection handlers, however, still returned the legacy `OwnerValidationErrors` (`{\"errors\":[...]}`) or a plain `String`.\n\n**Changed nine handlers** to build a `ProblemDetail` via the existing helper (which sets `type` = `about:blank`, `title` = exception simple name, `status`, and `detail`), passing the exception message as `detail`:\n\n- **400 Bad Request:** `MissingOwnerFields`, `DisposableEmailDomain`, `InvalidOwnerEmail`, `InvalidOwnerPostcode`, `InvalidOwnerTelephone`, `FutureRegistrationDate`\n- **409 Conflict:** `DuplicateOwnerIdentity`, `OwnerCityFull`\n- **429 Too Many Requests:** `OwnerDailyLimit`\n\nThe RFC7807-required members (`type`, `title`, `status`, `detail`) are all present, and status codes are preserved (each handler still sets its original `HttpStatus`). The `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectionIsProblemJson` test \u2014 which asserts `application/problem+json` and `$.status == 400` \u2014 passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS` is reported.\n\nNote: `OwnerValidationErrors` is now unused; I left it in place since removing it carries no benefit and touching it wasn't required.",
